   "url": "/projects/ai-business-analytics",
   "text": "AI Business Analytics (Applied machine learning; Working; Aug 2026). Upload a CSV and get cleaning, exploratory analysis, trained models, SHAP explanations and an LLM-written summary, packaged as an HTML and PDF report.\nStack: Python, scikit-learn, SHAP, Gemini, FastAPI, Streamlit, ReportLab.\nLinks: Source on GitHub https://github.com/Mokshitsharma/ai-business-analytics.\nAI Business Analytics: from a CSV to a written report\nUpload a business dataset and get cleaning, exploratory analysis, automatically trained models, SHAP explanations and an LLM-written summary, packaged as an HTML and PDF report.\nContext: For people who have a spreadsheet and a question but no analyst. The same pipeline runs from the command line, as a FastAPI service with background jobs, or in Streamlit.\nRole: Designed and built alone.\nStatus: Working, as a command-line tool, an API with background jobs and a Streamlit app.\nReport pipeline: Upload (CSV, Excel or JSON) -> Clean and profile -> Exploratory analysis -> Train and compare models -> SHAP explanations -> Written summary (Gemini; a structured recap if unavailable) -> HTML and PDF report\nDecision: The report still ships without the LLM. If the model is unavailable, the summary falls back to a structured recap of the findings rather than failing the job.\nDecision: One pipeline, three front doors. The command line, the API with background jobs the client polls, and Streamlit all call the same pipeline module.\nQuality: SHAP cost is bounded by explaining a 100-row sample, and analyses run as background jobs, so an upload never blocks a request."
